1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,969
People can follow a site without visiting it, by adding its feed to a feed reader.

2
00:00:05,969 --> 00:00:10,430
In this video, you enable the Feeds feature, check that Lists is enabled,

3
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:14,100
find the feed of a list, open it, and choose what it holds.

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,305
A feed is a page made for programs, listing the newest entries of a site.

5
00:00:23,305 --> 00:00:28,610
A feed reader checks the feeds a person follows and shows their entries in one place.

6
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,279
Two features work together.

7
00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:36,686
Feeds builds the feed in the RSS format and serves it, but publishes nothing by itself.

8
00:00:36,686 --> 00:00:40,930
Lists provides the lists whose items fill a feed, such as the posts

9
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:44,360
of a blog, and gives each list its own feed settings.

10
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:49,940
A list feed starts with the title, the address and the description of the list.

11
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:54,030
Then come the items of the list, newest first by creation date, up

12
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:55,678
to a number you choose.

13
00:00:55,678 --> 00:00:57,610
Only published items appear.

14
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,157
The page of a list carries a link to its feed.

15
00:01:01,157 --> 00:01:05,515
Browsers and feed readers can use that link to find the feed from the page.

16
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,420
The feed settings of the list control this link.

17
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:15,392
Feeds and Lists are separate features.

18
00:01:15,392 --> 00:01:19,460
Let's open Tools, Features, and type Feeds in the Search box.

19
00:01:19,951 --> 00:01:22,744
Feeds is listed under the Content category.

20
00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:23,826
Click Enable.

21
00:01:23,826 --> 00:01:28,271
The site restarts its features, and the Feeds row then shows the Enabled

22
00:01:28,271 --> 00:01:30,151
badge and a Disable button.

23
00:01:30,609 --> 00:01:34,945
Lists is under Content Management, and it shows the Enabled badge, so there

24
00:01:34,945 --> 00:01:36,176
is nothing to do.

25
00:01:36,176 --> 00:01:39,709
Both features must be enabled before a list can have a feed.

26
00:01:44,009 --> 00:01:49,034
To find the feed of a list, open Content, Content Items, and edit the Blog.

27
00:01:49,034 --> 00:01:51,329
A blog is a list of blog posts.

28
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:55,220
The editor of the Blog has three feed settings.

29
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:59,350
The first is a checkbox, Disable RSS feed link generation.

30
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:01,739
Unchecked means the feed is on.

31
00:02:02,195 --> 00:02:06,712
A hint under Feed proxy Url shows the current address of this feed.

32
00:02:06,712 --> 00:02:09,805
Click it, and the feed opens in another tab.

33
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:13,848
The feed is a page of structured text, written for programs.

34
00:02:13,848 --> 00:02:16,650
A feed reader turns it into a list of entries.

35
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:21,070
The page starts with the title, the address and the description of the Blog.

36
00:02:21,523 --> 00:02:25,826
After that comes one entry for each published post, newest first.

37
00:02:25,826 --> 00:02:29,522
An entry has a title, a link, the body of the post, and

38
00:02:29,522 --> 00:02:31,462
the date it was published.

39
00:02:31,462 --> 00:02:34,553
A post saved only as a draft is not included.

40
00:02:38,853 --> 00:02:42,983
In the editor, Feed items count sets how many entries the feed holds,

41
00:02:42,983 --> 00:02:44,635
and it starts at twenty.

42
00:02:44,635 --> 00:02:46,343
Let's change it to three.

43
00:02:46,798 --> 00:02:51,157
The feed reads the published version of the Blog, so click Publish.

44
00:02:51,157 --> 00:02:55,338
When the feed is reloaded, it holds only the three newest posts.

45
00:02:55,806 --> 00:03:00,896
Feed proxy Url takes a custom public address that proxies the local feed of the list.

46
00:03:00,896 --> 00:03:04,308
When it is set, the link in the page of the list points

47
00:03:04,308 --> 00:03:05,986
to that address instead.

48
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:10,470
To turn the feed off, publish the Blog with this checkbox checked:

49
00:03:10,470 --> 00:03:12,648
Disable RSS feed link generation.

50
00:03:12,648 --> 00:03:17,060
The page then has no link, and the feed address no longer returns a feed.

51
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:22,604
Feeds builds the feed, and Lists supplies its items.

52
00:03:22,604 --> 00:03:26,331
Enable both, set the options on a list, and publish it.

53
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:27,920
Thanks for watching.

